# IP routing for the peer interop tests.
#
# IPROUTE.SYS(8) route modes: d = datagram, v = virtual circuit
# (ip-over-ax25). Two stations, one of each, so both encapsulations can be
# exercised against the same node in the same run.
#
# Both need an explicit route as well as an ARP entry. An ARP entry alone is
# enough for XRouter to answer for its own address, but not for it to forward
# to a third party, which is what these tests ask it to do.

# Datagram: forwarded in UI frames, PID 0xCC.
arp add 44.131.20.1 ax25 AXTEST
ip route add 44.131.20.1 0.0.0.0 1 d

# Virtual circuit: XRouter opens an AX.25 session and sends the IP inside
# I-frames. This is the encapsulation LinBPQ cannot be used to test, because
# its virtual-circuit transmit is malformed on 64-bit.
arp add 44.131.20.2 ax25 AXVCT
ip route add 44.131.20.2 0.0.0.0 1 v
